@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 cluster: discovery, ownership, queue routing and Actor handoff

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #253746
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #334155
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #334155
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam participantFontColor #111827
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5CC
skinparam noteBorderColor #8A5A00
skinparam noteFontColor #111827
skinparam groupBorderColor #334155
skinparam groupHeaderBackgroundColor #E5E7EB
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam maxMessageSize 220

participant "Spring Boot Node" as Node
participant "ServiceInfoProvider" as Info
participant "ZkDiscoveryService" as Discovery
database "ZooKeeper /nodes" as ZK
participant "HashPartitionService" as Partition
participant "Spring Event Bus" as Events
participant "Core / RE Consumers" as Consumers
participant "ActorService" as ActorService
participant "Tenant / Device / Rule Actors" as Actors
participant "DefaultTbClusterService" as Cluster
queue "Queue Producer / Broker" as Broker
participant "Remote Owner Consumer" as Remote
participant "Remote Local Actor" as RemoteActor

== Service identity and registration ==
Node -> Info : @PostConstruct init()
Info -> Info : serviceId = configured or hostname\nserviceTypes from service.type\nassigned tenant profiles
Info -> Info : build ServiceInfo + system metrics
Node -> Info : @AfterContextReady setTransports()
Info -> Info : append transport bean names
Node -> Discovery : ApplicationReadyEvent
Discovery -> Info : getServiceInfo()
Info --> Discovery : protobuf ServiceInfo
Discovery -> ZK : create EPHEMERAL_SEQUENTIAL node
ZK --> Discovery : nodePath
Discovery -> ZK : PathChildrenCache current data
ZK --> Discovery : peers
Discovery -> Partition : recalculatePartitions(self, peers)

== Deterministic ownership calculation ==
Partition -> Partition : group services by QueueKey/type\nsort each list by serviceId
loop every QueueKey logical partition
  alt TB_RULE_ENGINE
    Partition -> Partition : choose dedicated profile candidates\nowner = (hash(tenantId)+partition) mod count
  else TB_CORE / VC
    Partition -> Partition : owner = partition mod count
  end
  Partition -> Partition : add index when owner == current ServiceInfo
end
Partition -> Events : PartitionChangeEvent per service type
Partition -> Events : ClusterTopologyChangeEvent if peer map changed
Partition -> Events : ServiceListChangedEvent always
Events -> Consumers : update subscribed physical topics
Events -> ActorService : PartitionChangeEvent
ActorService -> Actors : high-priority PartitionChangeMsg
alt Core partition revoked
  Actors -> Actors : stop Device Actors not in my partitions
else Rule Engine tenant revoked/acquired
  Actors -> Actors : destroy or initialize rule chains
end
note over Consumers,Actors
  Consumer subscriptions and Actor cleanup are separate listeners.
  Mailboxes, sessions and asynchronous side effects are not migrated.
end note

== Peer failure with restart debounce ==
ZK --> Discovery : CHILD_REMOVED(peer ServiceInfo)
Discovery -> Events : OtherServiceShutdownEvent immediately
Discovery -> Discovery : schedule recalc after zk.recalculate_delay
alt same serviceId returns before delay
  ZK --> Discovery : CHILD_ADDED(same serviceId)
  Discovery -> Discovery : cancel delayed task
else peer remains absent
  Discovery -> ZK : read current peers
  Discovery -> Partition : recalculatePartitions(self, peers)
end

== Cross-node Core or Rule Engine data message ==
Node -> Cluster : pushMsgToCore / pushMsgToRuleEngine
Cluster -> Partition : resolve(type, queueName, tenantId, entityId)
Partition -> Partition : entity UUID hash mod logical size
Partition --> Cluster : TopicPartitionInfo(full physical topic)
Cluster -> Broker : producer.send(Protobuf envelope, callback)
Broker --> Cluster : broker acknowledgement
Cluster --> Node : producer callback success
note over Node,Cluster
  This callback does not wait for the remote consumer,
  Actor, database or external side effect.
end note
Broker -> Remote : poll record on owned topic
Remote -> RemoteActor : local ActorSystem.tell(...)
RemoteActor --> Remote : business callback
Remote -> Broker : commit consumer position

== Per-service notification broadcast ==
Node -> Cluster : broadcast lifecycle/config notification
Cluster -> Partition : getAllServiceIds(target type)
Partition --> Cluster : serviceId set
loop each target serviceId
  Cluster -> Broker : send target notification topic
end
Broker -> Remote : target service notification consumer
Remote -> Remote : update local cache/session/runtime
note over Cluster,Remote
  Broadcast is N producer sends. A wrapper may aggregate producer callbacks,
  but never confirms that N consumers applied the update.
end note

== ZooKeeper session loss on current node ==
ZK --> Discovery : connection state LOST
Discovery -> Discovery : single-thread reconnect task
Discovery -> ZK : delete/close old client if possible
Discovery -> ZK : new client + blockUntilConnected
Discovery -> Info : generate updated ServiceInfo
Discovery -> ZK : publish new ephemeral sequential node
note over Discovery,ZK
  Peers may have already published shutdown and reassigned partitions.
  The returning node rebuilds from current topology; old in-memory work is not transferred.
end note
@enduml
